triage: revise_rules: The game file works as specified, but one thoughtless policy, always PAY until out of chips, beats random seats 59 of 60 times from both seat 1 and seat 2. The rules make refusing nearly free: an untaken card burns after two laps, so a steady payer dodges most cards. Chips paid also stay in the pot and get collected by the random players who take cards, which hurts the payer's opponents.

